course: dictionary
lesson: 12278
title: The word contribution
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A contribution is something you give to help. It might be money for a class present, or a share of the work when a group is making something. «Every child made a contribution to the class gift.» Each child gave something, and together it made the gift possible.
explain: The word can also mean the part someone plays in making something succeed. «Her contribution to the school project was a set of clear, careful notes.» Her notes helped the whole project work, so they were her share of it.
explain: Look at the words around contribution to find its meaning. Words like «money», «project», «group» or «class gift» are clues. Ask yourself: what was given, and who was it for? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A contribution is something you give to help pay for something or to help a group.
fact: A contribution can be money, time, ideas or work.
fact: Phrases to remember: make a contribution, a contribution to something, a big contribution.
fact: «Ben's contribution towards the trip was five pounds.» This means Ben gave five pounds to help pay for the trip.
fact: In maths, contributions are often added together to find a total, or shared out equally.
exercise: «Every child made a contribution to the class gift.» What is a contribution here? | *Something given to help | A long holiday | A loud noise | A type of game
exercise: «Ben's contribution towards the trip was five pounds.» What did Ben give? | A letter to his nan | *Money to help pay for the trip | A song | A cake for the teacher
exercise: Three friends each make a contribution of 4 pounds to a present. How much is the total? | 8 pounds | *12 pounds | 34 pounds | 7 pounds
test: «Her contribution to the project was a set of clear, careful notes.» In this sentence, contribution means: | A holiday she took last summer | A type of paint | *The part she played in making the project work | A shout of joy
test: Complete the phrase: make a big ___ to the group. | cabin | cushion | candle | *contribution
exam: «The magazine printed Amira's contribution, a poem about the sea.» In this sentence, contribution means: | *A piece of writing given to a magazine | A fish with a long tail | A new pair of shoes
